{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794539607401,"sessionID":"ses_e2d1cc122ffeqzrRrTg65W0LsJ","part":{"id":"prt_1d2e55569001rktl9LOgMzzSuP","sessionID":"ses_e2d1cc122ffeqzrRrTg65W0LsJ","messageID":"msg_1d2e54804001XmU1344V4Yo4k3","type":"step-start","snapshot":"a726d2b9c60b00fcc6257c77c2aadf5902e183a6"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794539623880,"sessionID":"ses_e2d1cc122ffeqzrRrTg65W0LsJ","part":{"partID":"prt_1d2e5556a0017eR1CGNIjXTUv5","sessionID":"ses_e2d1cc122ffeqzrRrTg65W0LsJ","messageID":"msg_1d2e54804001XmU1344V4Yo4k3","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-86314489c210f0c5","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"---\ntitle: \"Deep Research Strategy - offer-reach lineage, segment two\"\ndescription: \"Session tracking for the offer-reach lane of segment two: how often a plain chat request gets its command offered while false offers stay 0 of 35.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"offer reach research strategy\"\nimportance_tier: normal\ncontextType: planning\nversion: 1.14.0.19\n---\n\n# Deep Research Strategy - offer-reach\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n### Purpose\n\nPersistent brain for the offer-reach lineage of segment two. It tracks what to investigate, what worked, what failed and where to focus next. Read by the reducer and by each iteration of this lineage.\n\n### Usage\n\n- **Init:** populated with the topic, key questions and boundaries from this lineage's config.\n- **Per iteration:** this agent reads Next Focus, writes iteration evidence, and the reducer refreshes machine-owned sections.\n- **Mutability:** analyst-owned sections stay stable; machine-owned sections are rewritten by the reducer after each iteration.\n\n---\n\n## 2. TOPIC\nFind the next improvements to plain-chat command offering after phases 005, 006, 008 and 010 are built and phase 011 is in flight. The measured bottleneck is the offer rate, not obedience: the expected command was offered on 3 of 16 plain tune rows, /doctor:helper on 2 more, nothing on 11. Lane label `offer-reach`: hub mode vocabulary and deferral, a default command for a hub that defers, semantic lane weight and embedding text, the doctor family, and scoring thresholds. Floors that must not move: typed recall 24 of 44, false offers 0 of 35, scorer [159,50,20,5].\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\n\n- [ ] Which plain tune rows get no offer because a hub returns `defer` (or routes to a mode with no command), and what is the smallest rule that turns a deferring hub prompt into an offer without adding a false offer?\n- [ ] How much of the 3-of-16 plain offer rate is score placement (the command row or owner below the top-1 threshold) versus evidence absence (no lane, no phrase, no embedding text), measured per row?\n- [ ] What does the semantic lane contribute to the plain tune rows, and does a wording or weight change raise offers without moving the scorer floors?\n- [ ] Which doctor-family strings can ever score a document read, and how much plain recall is lost to the argued-route/document lookup rather than to scoring?\n- [ ] Which threshold or ranking constant could move the plain offer rate, and what is its measured risk to false offers 0 of 35 and typed recall 24 of 44?\n<!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n\n---\n\n## 4. NON-GOALS\n- Re-recommending anything phases 005, 006, 008, 010 built, or anything phase 011 plans (typed 44 of 44 delivery, policy on hub-attached commands, visibility guard, hook health, brief cost script, command document path in the head, Gate 2 policy clause, embed deadline abort, spawn collapse, brief-cost/read-cost scripts, native-spelling column).\n- Any change to code, commands, hooks or `AGENTS.md`; this lineage writes findings only, inside its own lineage directory.\n- Reading or printing holdout prompt text; reading the tune and none rows is allowed, holdout counts only.\n- Starting any model CLI session, arena or daemon, running ollama, or editing outside the lineage folder.\n\n---\n\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n- Convergence at newInfoRatio below 0.05 after minIterations 3.\n- Hard cap at 4 iterations.\n- Stop early only if the packet state is unreadable, which is an error status rather than convergence.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n## 6. ANSWERED QUESTIONS\n[None yet -- populated as iterations answer questions]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n## 7. WHAT WORKED\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n## 8. WHAT FAILED\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n[Populated when an approach has been tried from multiple angles without success]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n## 10. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n[Approaches investigated and definitively eliminated]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n## 10A. SATURATED DIRECTIONS AND DIVERGENCE FRONTIER\n- Completed pivots: 0\n- Failed pivots: 0\n- Audited overrides: 0\n- Saturated: none yet\n- Pivot lineage: none yet\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded\n<!-- /ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n## 11A. CARRIED-FORWARD OPEN QUESTIONS\n[Populated after iteration 1 completes]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n## 11. NEXT FOCUS\nIteration 1: enumerate the plain tune rows that got no offer and classify each one's cause in the advisor code (hub defer, threshold, missing evidence, doctor argued route).\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n## 12. KNOWN CONTEXT\n\nSegment one synthesis (`../009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/research.md`) ranked 14 items; ranks 1-6 and 10 became phase 010, and phase 011 builds rank 9 (second half), rank 12 and two items of rank 14, and explicitly defers rank 7, 8, 11 and 13. The offer bottleneck is new information from the after arm, not from segment one: segment one measured no offer at all before phase 005 and could not see offer rate.\n\nKnown surfaces for this lane:\n- Hub compiled routes: `.skilled/bin/compiled-route.cjs`, hub manifests under `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/` and `.skilled/skills/*/ROUTER.md`, `ADV/lib/compiled-routing-flag.ts`.\n- Command attach: `ADV/lib/command-attach.ts` (`MODE_COMMANDS`, `attachCommand`, depth gate, `commandRowFor`).\n- Scorer: `ADV/lib/scorer/lanes/explicit.ts` (`PHRASE_BOOSTS`, owner/row ordering), `ADV/lib/scorer/fusion.ts`, `ADV/lib/scorer/scoring-constants.ts`, `ADV/lib/scorer/lanes/semantic-shadow.ts`.\n- Corpus and captures: `ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-prompts.jsonl` (tune/none rows readable, holdout counts only), `capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs` (plain recall 9/45 phrases, 14/45 real embedder), `score-command-transcripts.mjs`, `run-command-behaviour.mjs`.\n- After-arm logs: `007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch/runs-pre-final.jsonl` and `runs-post-final.jsonl`, with `offeredCommand`/`offeredPolicy` per line.\n\n---\n\n## 13. RESEARCH BOUNDARIES\n- Max iterations: 4\n- Convergence threshold: 0.05\n- Per-iteration budget: 24 tool calls, 10 minutes\n- Progressive synthesis: true\n- research.md ownership: this lineage writes its own `research.md` as the workflow synthesis output; the parent merge owns the merged file\n- Lifecycle branches: `resume`, `restart` (live); `fork`, `completed-continue` (deferred)\n- Machine-owned sections: reducer controls Sections 3, 6, 7-11A\n- Canonical pause sentinel: `.deep-research-pause`\n- Current generation: 1\n- Started: 2026-11-13T10:00:00.000Z\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/offer-reach/deep-research-strategy.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/offer-reach/deep-research-strategy.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/offer-reach/deep-research-strategy.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"---\\ntitle: \\\"Deep Research Strategy - offer-reach lineage, segment two\\\"\\ndescription: \\\"Session tracking for the offer-reach lane of segment two: how often a plain chat request gets its command offered while false offers stay 0 of 35.\\\"\\ntrigger_phrases:\\n  - \\\"offer reach research strategy\\\"\\nimportance_tier: normal\\ncontextType: planning\\nversion: 1.14.0.19\\n---\\n\\n# Deep Research Strategy - offer-reach\\n\\n## 1. OVERVIEW\\n\\n### Purpose\\n\\nPersistent brain for the offer-reach lineage of segment two. It tracks what to investigate, what worked, what failed and where to focus next. Read by the reducer and by each iteration of this lineage.\\n\\n### Usage\\n\\n- **Init:** populated with the topic, key questions and boundaries from this lineage's config.\\n- **Per iteration:** this agent reads Next Focus, writes iteration evidence, and the reducer refreshes machine-owned sections.\\n- **Mutability:** analyst-owned sections stay stable; machine-owned sections are rewritten by the reducer after each iteration.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. TOPIC\\nFind the next improvements to plain-chat command offering after phases 005, 006, 008 and 010 are built and phase 011 is in flight. The measured bottleneck is the offer rate, not obedience: the expected command was offered on 3 of 16 plain tune rows, /doctor:helper on 2 more, nothing on 11. Lane label `offer-reach`: hub mode vocabulary and deferral, a default command for a hub that defers, semantic lane weight and embedding text, the doctor family, and scoring thresholds. Floors that must not move: typed recall 24 of 44, false offers 0 of 35, scorer [159,50,20,5].\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\\n## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\\n\\n- [ ] Which plain tune rows get no offer because a hub returns `defer` (or routes to a mode with no command), and what is the smallest rule that turns a deferring hub prompt into an offer without adding a false offer?\\n- [ ] How much of the 3-of-16 plain offer rate is score placement (the command row or owner below the top-1 threshold) versus evidence absence (no lane, no phrase, no embedding text), measured per row?\\n- [ ] What does the semantic lane contribute to the plain tune rows, and does a wording or weight change raise offers without moving the scorer floors?\\n- [ ] Which doctor-family strings can ever score a document read, and how much plain recall is lost to the argued-route/document lookup rather than to scoring?\\n- [ ] Which threshold or ranking constant could move the plain offer rate, and what is its measured risk to false offers 0 of 35 and typed recall 24 of 44?\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. NON-GOALS\\n- Re-recommending anything phases 005, 006, 008, 010 built, or anything phase 011 plans (typed 44 of 44 delivery, policy on hub-attached commands, visibility guard, hook health, brief cost script, command document path in the head, Gate 2 policy clause, embed deadline abort, spawn collapse, brief-cost/read-cost scripts, native-spelling column).\\n- Any change to code, commands, hooks or `AGENTS.md`; this lineage writes findings only, inside its own lineage directory.\\n- Reading or printing holdout prompt text; reading the tune and none rows is allowed, holdout counts only.\\n- Starting any model CLI session, arena or daemon, running ollama, or editing outside the lineage folder.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\\n- Convergence at newInfoRatio below 0.05 after minIterations 3.\\n- Hard cap at 4 iterations.\\n- Stop early only if the packet state is unreadable, which is an error status rather than convergence.\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\\n## 6. ANSWERED QUESTIONS\\n[None yet -- populated as iterations answer questions]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\\n## 7. WHAT WORKED\\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\\n## 8. WHAT FAILED\\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-failed -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\\n## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\\n[Populated when an approach has been tried from multiple angles without success]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\\n## 10. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\\n[Approaches investigated and definitively eliminated]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\\n## 10A. SATURATED DIRECTIONS AND DIVERGENCE FRONTIER\\n- Completed pivots: 0\\n- Failed pivots: 0\\n- Audited overrides: 0\\n- Saturated: none yet\\n- Pivot lineage: none yet\\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\\n## 11A. CARRIED-FORWARD OPEN QUESTIONS\\n[Populated after iteration 1 completes]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\\n## 11. NEXT FOCUS\\nIteration 1: enumerate the plain tune rows that got no offer and classify each one's cause in the advisor code (hub defer, threshold, missing evidence, doctor argued route).\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\\n## 12. KNOWN CONTEXT\\n\\nSegment one synthesis (`../009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/research.md`) ranked 14 items; ranks 1-6 and 10 became phase 010, and phase 011 builds rank 9 (second half), rank 12 and two items of rank 14, and explicitly defers rank 7, 8, 11 and 13. The offer bottleneck is new information from the after arm, not from segment one: segment one measured no offer at all before phase 005 and could not see offer rate.\\n\\nKnown surfaces for this lane:\\n- Hub compiled routes: `.skilled/bin/compiled-route.cjs`, hub manifests under `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/` and `.skilled/skills/*/ROUTER.md`, `ADV/lib/compiled-routing-flag.ts`.\\n- Command attach: `ADV/lib/command-attach.ts` (`MODE_COMMANDS`, `attachCommand`, depth gate, `commandRowFor`).\\n- Scorer: `ADV/lib/scorer/lanes/explicit.ts` (`PHRASE_BOOSTS`, owner/row ordering), `ADV/lib/scorer/fusion.ts`, `ADV/lib/scorer/scoring-constants.ts`, `ADV/lib/scorer/lanes/semantic-shadow.ts`.\\n- Corpus and captures: `ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-prompts.jsonl` (tune/none rows readable, holdout counts only), `capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs` (plain recall 9/45 phrases, 14/45 real embedder), `score-command-transcripts.mjs`, `run-command-behaviour.mjs`.\\n- After-arm logs: `007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch/runs-pre-final.jsonl` and `runs-post-final.jsonl`, with `offeredCommand`/`offeredPolicy` per line.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 13. RESEARCH BOUNDARIES\\n- Max iterations: 4\\n- Convergence threshold: 0.05\\n- Per-iteration budget: 24 tool calls, 10 minutes\\n- Progressive synthesis: true\\n- research.md ownership: this lineage writes its own `research.md` as the workflow synthesis output; the parent merge owns the merged file\\n- Lifecycle branches: `resume`, `restart` (live); `fork`, `completed-continue` (deferred)\\n- Machine-owned sections: reducer controls Sections 3, 6, 7-11A\\n- Canonical pause sentinel: `.deep-research-pause`\\n- Current generation: 1\\n- Started: 2026-11-13T10:00:00.000Z\\n\", \"path\": \"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/offer-reach/deep-research-strategy.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794539607402,"end":1794539623880}}}}
