{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794540069311,"sessionID":"ses_e2d1cc122ffeqzrRrTg65W0LsJ","part":{"partID":"prt_1d2ec5fbd002GUF1Bg5VUQ4d79","sessionID":"ses_e2d1cc122ffeqzrRrTg65W0LsJ","messageID":"msg_1d2ec4fbd001TNJaPwFBBWM15N","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-803bf70f68e77427","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n '290,400p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/lanes/semantic-shadow.ts"},"output":"      const score = cosineSimilarity(promptVector, skillVector);\n      const roundedScore = Math.round(score * 1_000_000) / 1_000_000;\n      return {\n        skillId,\n        lane: 'semantic_shadow' as const,\n        score: roundedScore,\n        evidence: [`cosine-exact:${score.toFixed(4)}`],\n        shadowOnly: false,\n      };\n    })\n    .filter((match): match is LaneMatch => match !== null);\n}\n\nexport function scoreSemanticShadowLane(prompt: string, projection: AdvisorProjection): LaneMatch[] {\n  if (projection.embeddingStaleness?.stale) {\n    setRuntimeHealth({ disabledReason: 'projection_embedding_stale' });\n    return [];\n  }\n\n  if (!activePromptEmbedding && process.env.VITEST === 'true') {\n    const tokens = tokenizePrompt(prompt);\n    return projection.skills\n      .map((skill) => ({\n        skillId: skill.id,\n        lane: 'semantic_shadow' as const,\n        score: Math.min(scoreTokenOverlap(tokens, [\n          skill.name,\n          skill.description,\n          ...skill.domains,\n          ...skill.intentSignals,\n          ...skill.derivedTriggers,\n        ]) * 0.8, 1),\n        evidence: ['shadow:test-fallback'],\n        shadowOnly: false,\n      }))\n      .filter((match) => match.score > 0.08);\n  }\n\n  const promptVector = activePromptEmbedding?.prompt === prompt\n    ? activePromptEmbedding.vector\n    : (projection.source === 'fixture' || process.env.VITEST === 'true' ? fixtureVector(prompt) : null);\n  if (!promptVector) {\n    return [];\n  }\n\n  const fixtureVectors = projection.source === 'fixture' || process.env.VITEST === 'true'\n    ? new Map(projection.skills.map((skill) => [skill.id, fixtureVector([\n        skill.name,\n        skill.description,\n        ...skill.domains,\n        ...skill.intentSignals,\n        ...skill.derivedTriggers,\n      ].join(' '))]))\n    : new Map<string, Float32Array>();\n\n  let cachedVectors = new Map<string, Float32Array>();\n  try {\n    cachedVectors = new Map(\n      loadSkillEmbeddings(projection.skills.map((skill) => skill.id))\n        .map((row) => [row.skillId, row.embedding]),\n    );\n  } catch (error: unknown) {\n    if (projection.source !== 'fixture') {\n      const message = error instanceof Error ? error.message : String(error);\n      setRuntimeHealth({ disabledReason: 'skill_embedding_load_failed' });\n      console.warn(`[semantic-shadow] Skill embedding load failed; cosine lane disabled (${message})`);\n      return [];\n    }\n  }\n\n  if (projection.source !== 'fixture' && process.env.VITEST !== 'true' && projection.skills.length > 0 && cachedVectors.size === 0) {\n    setRuntimeHealth({ disabledReason: 'no_skill_vectors' });\n  }\n\n  return projection.skills\n    .map((skill): LaneMatch | null => {\n      const skillVector = cachedVectors.get(skill.id) ?? fixtureVectors.get(skill.id);\n      if (!skillVector) {\n        return null;\n      }\n      const score = cosineSimilarity(promptVector, skillVector);\n      if (score <= COSINE_THRESHOLD) {\n        return null;\n      }\n\n      // The cutoff suppresses random near-zero vector noise. The semantic lane is\n      // LIVE in the registry (weight 0.05, live=true), so the raw match tags\n      // shadowOnly:false to match lane liveness. Fusion independently derives the\n      // effective shadowOnly from isLiveScorerLane, so the two values now agree and\n      // any direct reader of the raw LaneMatch sees the same answer as attribution.\n      const roundedScore = Math.round(score * 1_000_000) / 1_000_000;\n      return {\n        skillId: skill.id,\n        lane: 'semantic_shadow' as const,\n        score: roundedScore,\n        evidence: [`cosine:${score.toFixed(4)}`],\n        shadowOnly: false,\n      };\n    })\n    .filter((match): match is LaneMatch => match !== null);\n}\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"      const score = cosineSimilarity(promptVector, skillVector);\n      const roundedScore = Math.round(score * 1_000_000) / 1_000_000;\n      return {\n        skillId,\n        lane: 'semantic_shadow' as const,\n        score: roundedScore,\n        evidence: [`cosine-exact:${score.toFixed(4)}`],\n        shadowOnly: false,\n      };\n    })\n    .filter((match): match is LaneMatch => match !== null);\n}\n\nexport function scoreSemanticShadowLane(prompt: string, projection: AdvisorProjection): LaneMatch[] {\n  if (projection.embeddingStaleness?.stale) {\n    setRuntimeHealth({ disabledReason: 'projection_embedding_stale' });\n    return [];\n  }\n\n  if (!activePromptEmbedding && process.env.VITEST === 'true') {\n    const tokens = tokenizePrompt(prompt);\n    return projection.skills\n      .map((skill) => ({\n        skillId: skill.id,\n        lane: 'semantic_shadow' as const,\n        score: Math.min(scoreTokenOverlap(tokens, [\n          skill.name,\n          skill.description,\n          ...skill.domains,\n          ...skill.intentSignals,\n          ...skill.derivedTriggers,\n        ]) * 0.8, 1),\n        evidence: ['shadow:test-fallback'],\n        shadowOnly: false,\n      }))\n      .filter((match) => match.score > 0.08);\n  }\n\n  const promptVector = activePromptEmbedding?.prompt === prompt\n    ? activePromptEmbedding.vector\n    : (projection.source === 'fixture' || process.env.VITEST === 'true' ? fixtureVector(prompt) : null);\n  if (!promptVector) {\n    return [];\n  }\n\n  const fixtureVectors = projection.source === 'fixture' || process.env.VITEST === 'true'\n    ? new Map(projection.skills.map((skill) => [skill.id, fixtureVector([\n        skill.name,\n        skill.description,\n        ...skill.domains,\n        ...skill.intentSignals,\n        ...skill.derivedTriggers,\n      ].join(' '))]))\n    : new Map<string, Float32Array>();\n\n  let cachedVectors = new Map<string, Float32Array>();\n  try {\n    cachedVectors = new Map(\n      loadSkillEmbeddings(projection.skills.map((skill) => skill.id))\n        .map((row) => [row.skillId, row.embedding]),\n    );\n  } catch (error: unknown) {\n    if (projection.source !== 'fixture') {\n      const message = error instanceof Error ? error.message : String(error);\n      setRuntimeHealth({ disabledReason: 'skill_embedding_load_failed' });\n      console.warn(`[semantic-shadow] Skill embedding load failed; cosine lane disabled (${message})`);\n      return [];\n    }\n  }\n\n  if (projection.source !== 'fixture' && process.env.VITEST !== 'true' && projection.skills.length > 0 && cachedVectors.size === 0) {\n    setRuntimeHealth({ disabledReason: 'no_skill_vectors' });\n  }\n\n  return projection.skills\n    .map((skill): LaneMatch | null => {\n      const skillVector = cachedVectors.get(skill.id) ?? fixtureVectors.get(skill.id);\n      if (!skillVector) {\n        return null;\n      }\n      const score = cosineSimilarity(promptVector, skillVector);\n      if (score <= COSINE_THRESHOLD) {\n        return null;\n      }\n\n      // The cutoff suppresses random near-zero vector noise. The semantic lane is\n      // LIVE in the registry (weight 0.05, live=true), so the raw match tags\n      // shadowOnly:false to match lane liveness. Fusion independently derives the\n      // effective shadowOnly from isLiveScorerLane, so the two values now agree and\n      // any direct reader of the raw LaneMatch sees the same answer as attribution.\n      const roundedScore = Math.round(score * 1_000_000) / 1_000_000;\n      return {\n        skillId: skill.id,\n        lane: 'semantic_shadow' as const,\n        score: roundedScore,\n        evidence: [`cosine:${score.toFixed(4)}`],\n        shadowOnly: false,\n      };\n    })\n    .filter((match): match is LaneMatch => match !== null);\n}\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n '290,400p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/lanes/semantic-shadow.ts\"}"},"time":{"start":1794540068797,"end":1794540069311}}}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1794540070767,"sessionID":"ses_e2d1cc122ffeqzrRrTg65W0LsJ","part":{"id":"prt_1d2ec676f0019JaNJaWbpeSOQR","sessionID":"ses_e2d1cc122ffeqzrRrTg65W0LsJ","messageID":"msg_1d2ec4fbd001TNJaPwFBBWM15N","type":"step-finish","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"46cb58eca31f65ee518284957a2b5fbdf7a24836","cost":0,"tokens":{"input":1222,"output":92,"reasoning":167,"cache":{"read":155904,"write":0}}}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794540073340,"sessionID":"ses_e2d1cc122ffeqzrRrTg65W0LsJ","part":{"id":"prt_1d2ec717c001HjUg5bAAlaCZMF","sessionID":"ses_e2d1cc122ffeqzrRrTg65W0LsJ","messageID":"msg_1d2ec67760016Fr0tQM2XB4cTU","type":"step-start","snapshot":"a455bff1a1dd400a0f7e7a2eb95f8dbb5ccdca2b"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794540103421,"sessionID":"ses_e2d1cc122ffeqzrRrTg65W0LsJ","part":{"partID":"prt_1d2ec98de002un7NhJHPSiXDAi","sessionID":"ses_e2d1cc122ffeqzrRrTg65W0LsJ","messageID":"msg_1d2ec67760016Fr0tQM2XB4cTU","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8f1148586aed9420","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Iteration 2: Placement versus evidence, and what the semantic lane actually buys\n\n## Focus\n\nDecompose the rows whose top skill is not the command's owner (`create-command`, `create-goal`, `create-manual-testing-playbook`, `deep-review`, `doctor-deep-loop`) into score placement versus evidence absence, and measure what the semantic lane contributes to the plain tune split and to the 16-row chat set. Deferred alternatives from iteration 1: whether a threshold change could substitute for per-row evidence (it cannot, see finding 3).\n\n## Actions Taken\n\n1. Compared the committed stand-in capture (`command-routing-baseline.json`) with the real-embedder capture (`008-embedder-setup-and-cost/scratch/real-embedding-after.json`) row by row over the 45 plain tune rows.\n2. Read the explicit lane's `PHRASE_BOOSTS`, `TOKEN_BOOSTS`, the fusion calibration rules (`createAgent`, `createTestingPlaybook`, `speckitResume`, `reviewLoop`) and the command meaning gate (`COMMAND_MEANING_MIN_COSINE`, `COMMAND_MEANING_MARGIN`, `commandMeaningEligible`).\n3. Read the semantic lane's weight, cosine cutoff, deadline and embedded text source (`skill.name`, `description`, `domains`, `intentSignals`, `derivedTriggers` from the skill-graph DB).\n4. Read phase 003's implementation summary for the previously attempted alias changes and their measured outcome.\n5. Re-read the 31 none rows for the phrases proposed in this iteration.\n\n## Findings\n\n1. The real embedder lifts plain tune recall from 9 of 45 to 14 of 45, but the five gained rows are `cmd-doctor-env`, `cmd-doctor-git`, `cmd-doctor-symlink`, `cmd-speckit-handoff` and `cmd-speckit-plan` — none of them in the 16-row chat set. The chat set's five delivered offers are all attached (hub route or doctor handoff), and its own-row recall is 0. So the semantic lane's measured gain is orthogonal to the chat bottleneck: a weight or threshold change to that lane cannot explain or fix the 3-of-16. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/008-embedder-setup-and-cost/scratch/real-embedding-after.json] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-routing-baseline.json] [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch/runs-post-final.jsonl]\n\n2. A command may pass on meaning only when its real cosine clears 0.72 and leads the strongest other command by 0.02, and the semantic lane's weight is 0.05; the anchor then lifts the row to the confidence threshold. The embedded text per skill is the projection's name, description, domains, intent signals and derived triggers loaded from the skill-graph DB, so improving meaning for a command means enriching that row's metadata and re-embedding — there are no per-command paraphrase exemplars today. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:846] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:921] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/lanes/semantic-shadow.ts:322] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/lanes/semantic-shadow.ts:376]\n\n3. Four of the five wrong-top rows are evidence absence, not placement: `create-command` has no `/create:command` phrase and the `prompt` token lifts sk-prompt; `create-goal` has no \"intent file\" evidence and system-spec-kit wins; `create-manual-testing-playbook`'s boost keys require the literal \"manual testing playbook\" or \"create a test playbook\" and the row says \"test script package\"; `deep-review`'s wording has `audit` lifting sk-code and no deep-loop phrase at all. Only `create-agent-01` is placement-like (its aliases fired, `/create:agent` sits in the top-3, but the hub answers `clarify`), and `doctor-deep-loop` is a hub gap rather than a score margin. A lower threshold therefore converts none of them. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/lanes/explicit.ts:28] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:827] [INFERENCE: baseline top values crossed with the prompt text and the boost keys, tune rows only]\n\n4. Generic alias widening is a proven dead end on this corpus. Phase 003 added \"persona file\" to the sk-doc agent aliases and removed it again because it attached `/create:agent` to \"update the customer persona file for the marketing site\"; tune combined reach fell from 10 to 9 of 45. Any new alias has to be narrower than the generic noun phrase — \"specialist persona file\" or \"agent definition\", not \"persona file\". [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/003-plain-chat-command-reach/implementation-summary.md:140]\n\n5. The cheapest evidence fix that does not depend on the embedder is a multi-word explicit anchor per row: \"agent definition\" and \"specialist persona file\" for `/create:agent`, \"prompt shortcut\" and \"argument-hint\" for `/create:command`, \"intent file\" for `/create:goal`, \"test script package\" and \"walk through by hand\" for `/create:manual-testing-playbook`, \"many passes\" and \"findings stop changing\" for `/deep:review`. Each phrase is absent from all 31 none rows, and each is literal, so the change is measurable with the stand-in capture. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-prompts.jsonl] [INFERENCE: phrase absence checked against the 31 readable none rows]\n\n6. The only lever that generalizes past literal phrasing is metadata enrichment plus re-embedding: add paraphrase exemplars to the command rows' intent signals in `command-metadata.json` and rebuild the skill-graph vectors, then measure with `--real-embedding`. It is also the only lever this lineage cannot verify, because running the embedder is out of scope; it belongs to the phase that owns the next capture. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/lanes/semantic-shadow.ts:349]\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- Lowering `COMMAND_MEANING_MIN_COSINE` below 0.72: it cannot reach a row with no cosine evidence, and the 5 real-embedder gains are outside the chat set.\n- Raising the semantic lane weight: the lane is live at 0.05 and its gains are already counted; a weight change would reorder rows the floor depends on without adding evidence.\n- Re-adding \"persona file\": measured regression in phase 003 (finding 4).\n- Treating `doctor-deep-loop` as a scoring miss: the deep hub declares no doctor mode, so there is no command candidate to rank.\n\n## Dead Ends\n\n- Threshold tuning as a substitute for evidence: four of five rows are below top-3, so no threshold reaches them.\n- A second meaning lane with a lower cosine bar: it would spend false-offer risk on the doctor and speckit rows that already pass, not on the chat rows.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- Ambiguous input: \"evidence absence\" is scored as \"the command row is absent from top-3 and no phrase or command-literal anchor exists\"; \"placement\" is \"the row is in top-3 but not top-1\".\n- Contradictory evidence: the prompt brief cites plain recall 14 of 45 with the real embedder while the committed stand-in capture reads 9 of 45; both are correct for their regime, and the difference is exactly the five rows named in finding 1.\n- Missing dependencies: the advisor dist is stale, so no live capture could be rerun; all row facts come from committed captures.\n- Partial success: the static decomposition is complete; the proposed anchors are reasoned against the none rows but not measured.\n\n## Sources Consulted\n\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/008-embedder-setup-and-cost/scratch/real-embedding-after.json`\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/008-embedder-setup-and-cost/scratch/verification-evidence.txt`\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/003-plain-chat-command-reach/implementation-summary.md`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-routing-baseline.json`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-prompts.jsonl`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/lanes/explicit.ts`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/scoring-constants.ts`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/lanes/semantic-shadow.ts`\n\n## Assessment\n\n- New information ratio: 0.85\n- Questions addressed: KQ2, KQ3\n- Questions answered: KQ2 (4 of 5 are evidence absence), KQ3 (the semantic lane adds 5 rows, all outside the chat set)\n\n## Reflection\n\n- What worked and why: diffing the two captures row by row turned a headline \"9 to 14\" into a per-row fact, which is what showed the gain is orthogonal to the chat set; reading phase 003's summary recovered a measured alias regression that would otherwise have been re-proposed.\n- What did not work and why: the stand-in capture cannot expose cosine values, so the exact distance from 0.72 for each chat row stays unknown without a re-embed.\n- What I would do differently: start from the per-row diff rather than the headline metrics, because aggregate recall hides which prompts move.\n\n## Questions Answered\n\n- KQ2: four of the five wrong-top rows are evidence absence; only create-agent-01 is placement-like and doctor-deep-loop is a hub gap.\n- KQ3: the semantic lane contributes five tune rows (doctor env/git/symlink, speckit handoff/plan), none in the chat set, so its present configuration does not move the 3-of-16.\n\n## Questions Remaining\n\n- Which of the proposed explicit anchors can be added without moving any none row, and what is each anchor's measured tune gain in the stand-in capture?\n- Can the doctor family gain a deep-loop diagnostic route without breaking the deep hub's defer contract?\n\n## Recommended Next Focus\n\nIteration 3: the doctor family and the deep-family defer — enumerate every doctor chat row's path, test whether a doctor handoff for deep-loop diagnostics and a `ask`-only defer offer close the three remaining deep/doctor misses, and check each against the none rows.\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/offer-reach/iterations/iteration-002.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/offer-reach/iterations/iteration-002.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/offer-reach/iterations/iteration-002.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"# Iteration 2: Placement versus evidence, and what the semantic lane actually buys\\n\\n## Focus\\n\\nDecompose the rows whose top skill is not the command's owner (`create-command`, `create-goal`, `create-manual-testing-playbook`, `deep-review`, `doctor-deep-loop`) into score placement versus evidence absence, and measure what the semantic lane contributes to the plain tune split and to the 16-row chat set. Deferred alternatives from iteration 1: whether a threshold change could substitute for per-row evidence (it cannot, see finding 3).\\n\\n## Actions Taken\\n\\n1. Compared the committed stand-in capture (`command-routing-baseline.json`) with the real-embedder capture (`008-embedder-setup-and-cost/scratch/real-embedding-after.json`) row by row over the 45 plain tune rows.\\n2. Read the explicit lane's `PHRASE_BOOSTS`, `TOKEN_BOOSTS`, the fusion calibration rules (`createAgent`, `createTestingPlaybook`, `speckitResume`, `reviewLoop`) and the command meaning gate (`COMMAND_MEANING_MIN_COSINE`, `COMMAND_MEANING_MARGIN`, `commandMeaningEligible`).\\n3. Read the semantic lane's weight, cosine cutoff, deadline and embedded text source (`skill.name`, `description`, `domains`, `intentSignals`, `derivedTriggers` from the skill-graph DB).\\n4. Read phase 003's implementation summary for the previously attempted alias changes and their measured outcome.\\n5. Re-read the 31 none rows for the phrases proposed in this iteration.\\n\\n## Findings\\n\\n1. The real embedder lifts plain tune recall from 9 of 45 to 14 of 45, but the five gained rows are `cmd-doctor-env`, `cmd-doctor-git`, `cmd-doctor-symlink`, `cmd-speckit-handoff` and `cmd-speckit-plan` — none of them in the 16-row chat set. The chat set's five delivered offers are all attached (hub route or doctor handoff), and its own-row recall is 0. So the semantic lane's measured gain is orthogonal to the chat bottleneck: a weight or threshold change to that lane cannot explain or fix the 3-of-16. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/008-embedder-setup-and-cost/scratch/real-embedding-after.json] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-routing-baseline.json] [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch/runs-post-final.jsonl]\\n\\n2. A command may pass on meaning only when its real cosine clears 0.72 and leads the strongest other command by 0.02, and the semantic lane's weight is 0.05; the anchor then lifts the row to the confidence threshold. The embedded text per skill is the projection's name, description, domains, intent signals and derived triggers loaded from the skill-graph DB, so improving meaning for a command means enriching that row's metadata and re-embedding — there are no per-command paraphrase exemplars today. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:846] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:921] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/lanes/semantic-shadow.ts:322] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/lanes/semantic-shadow.ts:376]\\n\\n3. Four of the five wrong-top rows are evidence absence, not placement: `create-command` has no `/create:command` phrase and the `prompt` token lifts sk-prompt; `create-goal` has no \\\"intent file\\\" evidence and system-spec-kit wins; `create-manual-testing-playbook`'s boost keys require the literal \\\"manual testing playbook\\\" or \\\"create a test playbook\\\" and the row says \\\"test script package\\\"; `deep-review`'s wording has `audit` lifting sk-code and no deep-loop phrase at all. Only `create-agent-01` is placement-like (its aliases fired, `/create:agent` sits in the top-3, but the hub answers `clarify`), and `doctor-deep-loop` is a hub gap rather than a score margin. A lower threshold therefore converts none of them. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/lanes/explicit.ts:28] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:827] [INFERENCE: baseline top values crossed with the prompt text and the boost keys, tune rows only]\\n\\n4. Generic alias widening is a proven dead end on this corpus. Phase 003 added \\\"persona file\\\" to the sk-doc agent aliases and removed it again because it attached `/create:agent` to \\\"update the customer persona file for the marketing site\\\"; tune combined reach fell from 10 to 9 of 45. Any new alias has to be narrower than the generic noun phrase — \\\"specialist persona file\\\" or \\\"agent definition\\\", not \\\"persona file\\\". [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/003-plain-chat-command-reach/implementation-summary.md:140]\\n\\n5. The cheapest evidence fix that does not depend on the embedder is a multi-word explicit anchor per row: \\\"agent definition\\\" and \\\"specialist persona file\\\" for `/create:agent`, \\\"prompt shortcut\\\" and \\\"argument-hint\\\" for `/create:command`, \\\"intent file\\\" for `/create:goal`, \\\"test script package\\\" and \\\"walk through by hand\\\" for `/create:manual-testing-playbook`, \\\"many passes\\\" and \\\"findings stop changing\\\" for `/deep:review`. Each phrase is absent from all 31 none rows, and each is literal, so the change is measurable with the stand-in capture. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-prompts.jsonl] [INFERENCE: phrase absence checked against the 31 readable none rows]\\n\\n6. The only lever that generalizes past literal phrasing is metadata enrichment plus re-embedding: add paraphrase exemplars to the command rows' intent signals in `command-metadata.json` and rebuild the skill-graph vectors, then measure with `--real-embedding`. It is also the only lever this lineage cannot verify, because running the embedder is out of scope; it belongs to the phase that owns the next capture. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/lanes/semantic-shadow.ts:349]\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- Lowering `COMMAND_MEANING_MIN_COSINE` below 0.72: it cannot reach a row with no cosine evidence, and the 5 real-embedder gains are outside the chat set.\\n- Raising the semantic lane weight: the lane is live at 0.05 and its gains are already counted; a weight change would reorder rows the floor depends on without adding evidence.\\n- Re-adding \\\"persona file\\\": measured regression in phase 003 (finding 4).\\n- Treating `doctor-deep-loop` as a scoring miss: the deep hub declares no doctor mode, so there is no command candidate to rank.\\n\\n## Dead Ends\\n\\n- Threshold tuning as a substitute for evidence: four of five rows are below top-3, so no threshold reaches them.\\n- A second meaning lane with a lower cosine bar: it would spend false-offer risk on the doctor and speckit rows that already pass, not on the chat rows.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- Ambiguous input: \\\"evidence absence\\\" is scored as \\\"the command row is absent from top-3 and no phrase or command-literal anchor exists\\\"; \\\"placement\\\" is \\\"the row is in top-3 but not top-1\\\".\\n- Contradictory evidence: the prompt brief cites plain recall 14 of 45 with the real embedder while the committed stand-in capture reads 9 of 45; both are correct for their regime, and the difference is exactly the five rows named in finding 1.\\n- Missing dependencies: the advisor dist is stale, so no live capture could be rerun; all row facts come from committed captures.\\n- Partial success: the static decomposition is complete; the proposed anchors are reasoned against the none rows but not measured.\\n\\n## Sources Consulted\\n\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/008-embedder-setup-and-cost/scratch/real-embedding-after.json`\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/008-embedder-setup-and-cost/scratch/verification-evidence.txt`\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/003-plain-chat-command-reach/implementation-summary.md`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-routing-baseline.json`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-prompts.jsonl`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/lanes/explicit.ts`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/scoring-constants.ts`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/lanes/semantic-shadow.ts`\\n\\n## Assessment\\n\\n- New information ratio: 0.85\\n- Questions addressed: KQ2, KQ3\\n- Questions answered: KQ2 (4 of 5 are evidence absence), KQ3 (the semantic lane adds 5 rows, all outside the chat set)\\n\\n## Reflection\\n\\n- What worked and why: diffing the two captures row by row turned a headline \\\"9 to 14\\\" into a per-row fact, which is what showed the gain is orthogonal to the chat set; reading phase 003's summary recovered a measured alias regression that would otherwise have been re-proposed.\\n- What did not work and why: the stand-in capture cannot expose cosine values, so the exact distance from 0.72 for each chat row stays unknown without a re-embed.\\n- What I would do differently: start from the per-row diff rather than the headline metrics, because aggregate recall hides which prompts move.\\n\\n## Questions Answered\\n\\n- KQ2: four of the five wrong-top rows are evidence absence; only create-agent-01 is placement-like and doctor-deep-loop is a hub gap.\\n- KQ3: the semantic lane contributes five tune rows (doctor env/git/symlink, speckit handoff/plan), none in the chat set, so its present configuration does not move the 3-of-16.\\n\\n## Questions Remaining\\n\\n- Which of the proposed explicit anchors can be added without moving any none row, and what is each anchor's measured tune gain in the stand-in capture?\\n- Can the doctor family gain a deep-loop diagnostic route without breaking the deep hub's defer contract?\\n\\n## Recommended Next Focus\\n\\nIteration 3: the doctor family and the deep-family defer — enumerate every doctor chat row's path, test whether a doctor handoff for deep-loop diagnostics and a `ask`-only defer offer close the three remaining deep/doctor misses, and check each against the none rows.\\n\", \"path\": \"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/offer-reach/iterations/iteration-002.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794540083422,"end":1794540103421}}}}
