{"type":"text","timestamp":1794540566182,"sessionID":"ses_e2d1cc122ffeqzrRrTg65W0LsJ","part":{"id":"prt_1d2f3e232002RHUvlGnZi2JrU1","sessionID":"ses_e2d1cc122ffeqzrRrTg65W0LsJ","messageID":"msg_1d2f3d817001Ve2iastDGZ6jZI","type":"text","text":"## Lineage `offer-reach` complete — 4 iterations, stop reason `maxIterationsReached`\n\n**What was measured and found**\n\n- The 16 plain tune rows in the after arm delivered **5 offers** (3 exact create commands, 2 generic `/doctor:helper`), not the capture's 6 — the capture's `offered` flag counts top-3 presence while the renderer prints only the top recommendation. `offeredCommand` in the run log is the delivered truth.\n- **Every delivered plain offer travels through a compiled hub route or the doctor handoff.** No plain row has a command row on top.\n- `sk-doc` routes only 3 of 9 create chat rows to a command mode; its vocabulary is paraphrase-blind (\"agent definition\", \"specialist persona file\", \"before and after my rewrite\", \"overview page\", \"hub skill\" all miss). Phase 003 already proved generic \"persona file\" widening causes a wrong offer, so aliases must be task-shaped.\n- The doctor matcher already ranks the right command (`/doctor:agents-md` 12.781, `/doctor:ci` 12.301, `/doctor:deep-loop` 16.249) and the handoff still names `/doctor:helper`; the deep-loop row never reaches the matcher because the strong-cue list lacks \"stopped converging\".\n- The real embedder's 9→14 of 45 gain is **orthogonal** to the chat set: all five gained rows are doctor env/git/symlink and speckit handoff/plan.\n- A defer-time default command is unsafe — it fires on `nm-system-deep-loop-01`, which must stay silent.\n\n**Ranked recommendations** (in `research.md` §9): 1) doctor specific-command handoff + cues (4 rows, measured matcher scores, low risk); 2) `sk-doc` paraphrase aliases (3 chat rows + 5 wider tune rows, data-only, canary-checked); 3) deep scorer-anchor + hub-alias pair (3 rows, medium risk); 4) explicit command anchors for the three wrong-top create rows (medium risk); 5) metadata re-embed (unmeasurable here).\n\n**Files written** (all inside `specs/.../lineages/offer-reach/`): `iterations/iteration-001..004.md`, `deltas/iter-001..004.jsonl`, `research.md`, `resource-map.md`, `deep-research-config.json` (status `complete`), `deep-research-strategy.md`, `findings-registry.json`, `deep-research-dashboard.md`; every state row went through `append-mode-event.cjs` (6 ledger frames, 0 pending) and `reduce-state.cjs` ran after each iteration (0 corruption).\n\n**Verification**: 4 iteration records with ratios 0.90/0.85/0.88/0.70; 6 findings per delta; all narratives carry the required sections and citations; 5/5 lane key questions ticked; no direct state-log write; no model/arena/daemon started; no writes outside the lineage in the repository.\n\n**Deviations recorded**: `spec.md` write-back and post-synthesis `validate.sh` were skipped because both are outside this lineage's write authority; the capture could not be rerun because the advisor dist is stale and rebuilding writes outside the lineage, so expected row gains are inferred and labelled as such; scratch computations used `/tmp` files outside the repository.\n\nFANOUT_LINEAGE_COMPLETE:offer-reach","time":{"start":1794540560946,"end":1794540566182}}}
